# Example config for `bench_and_profile.sh <label>`.
#
# Copy this file to configs/<your-label>.env and edit the knobs for the
# change you're testing, then run:
#
#   benchmark/bench_and_profile.sh <your-label>
#
# bench_and_profile.sh sources configs/<label>.env (if present) before
# launching the engine, so "make a change -> new label -> one command" is
# just: pick a label, drop the env knobs here, run the wrapper.
#
# Every var below is optional -- bench_and_profile.sh falls back to the same
# defaults launch_unieinfra.sh / run_sweep.sh already use. Only set what
# you're actually changing versus the baseline, so the diff against
# results/unieinfra/clean/ (or whatever --baseline you pick) stays legible.

# --- what to serve ---
# MODEL=/workspace/models/Qwen/Qwen3-8B
# GPU=1
# PORT=8010

# --- launch_unieinfra.sh knobs (see benchmark/launch/launch_unieinfra.sh) ---
# DTYPE=bfloat16
# ATTN=triton                 # triton | flashinfer | ...
# MAX_NUM_SEQS=256
# MAX_CGRAPH=256
# DISABLE_RADIX=0             # keep prefix cache ON unless you're specifically testing it off
#
# Forward-compatible passthrough: bench_and_profile.sh does not hardcode the
# launch script's flag list, so any NEW env knob launch_unieinfra.sh grows
# later (e.g. QUANTIZATION, KV_CACHE_DTYPE, ENABLE_ADAPTIVE_BATCH -- seen in
# some hand-run investigations under results/unieinfra/fp8w_fixed and
# results/unieinfra/abl_baseline, not yet wired into launch_unieinfra.sh
# itself) can already be set here once the launch script picks it up.

# --- run_sweep.sh hygiene knobs (see benchmark/run_sweep.sh; usually leave these alone
# so runs stay comparable) ---
# CONCURRENCIES="1 16 32 64 128 256"
# ILEN=1024
# OLEN=256
# PROMPTS_PER_CONC=8
# WARMUPS=8
# SEED=0
# FLUSH=1

# --- bench_and_profile.sh's own knobs ---
# BASELINE=clean               # unieinfra label to diff against + flag regressions on
# PROFILE=1                    # set 0 to skip the profile_hot_decode.py step
# CONTAINER=unieinfra-dev
